# Unread counts a message unless its buffer is focused in an active
# window. Focusing a buffer clears its counters; so does the window
# becoming active again with the buffer focused.
! welcome
< :textual!u@h JOIN #a
> MODE #a
< :textual!u@h JOIN #b
> MODE #b
? focus console
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #a :one
? unread #a 1 highlights 0
! focus #a
? focus #a
? unread #a 0 highlights 0
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #a :two textual
? unread #a 0 highlights 0
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #b :three
? unread #b 1 highlights 0
# Focusing what is focused changes nothing.
! focus #a
? focus #a
! window inactive
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #a :four textual
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #a :five
? unread #a 2 highlights 1
! window active
? unread #a 0 highlights 0
? unread #b 1 highlights 0
! window inactive
! focus #b
? unread #b 1 highlights 0
! window active
? unread #b 0 highlights 0
? registered textual
